+## Fixes found only by an actual Qt4 compile (post-export)
+
+The items below were found and fixed *after* the branch first went to the
+user for a real MacPorts/Qt4 build — i.e. by the Phase 0 oracle this branch
+never got to run locally. Listed here because they reveal real blind spots
+in the static-analysis approach above, not just isolated bugs:
+
+- **`connect (` with a space before the paren** (`d065cb96`) — every
+  grep-based completeness check in this document and in the original task
+  spec used a literal `connect\(` pattern with no whitespace tolerance, so
+  `src/Plugins/AbookAddressbook/AbookAddressbook.cpp:122`'s
+  `connect (m_filesystemWatcher, &QFileSystemWatcher::fileChanged, ...)`
+  silently survived every audit. If re-running the completeness checklist
+  below, use `connect\s*\(`/`disconnect\s*\(`, not a bare-paren pattern.
+- **`QByteArrayLiteral`** (`a4f0d1f7`) — the Qt5-only sibling of
+  `QStringLiteral`; the original audit table only ever listed
+  `QStringLiteral`. Shimmed the same way in `src/Common/Qt4Compat.h`.
+- **`QMap<QByteArray,QByteArray>` metatype** (`a4f0d1f7`, `542b3bef`) — Qt5
+  auto-derives `QMetaType` for template containers of already-registered
+  value types; Qt4 has no such mechanism. Needed an explicit
+  `Q_DECLARE_METATYPE`/`qRegisterMetaType`, same as the codebase already
+  does for the sibling `QList<QByteArray>`. The first attempt at this fix
+  broke the build a *second* way — `Q_DECLARE_METATYPE` is a
+  single-argument macro, so the unparenthesized comma inside
+  `QMap<QByteArray, QByteArray>` split into two macro arguments; fixed with
+  a typedef (the standard workaround). Not Qt4-specific — would have broken
+  Qt5 identically.
+- **`src/Cryptography/{MessageModel,MessagePart}.{cpp,h}`** (`970e81b1`) —
+  the biggest scope correction. `CMakeLists.txt:362-366` adds
+  `MessageModel.cpp`/`MessagePart.cpp`/`PartReplacer.cpp` to
+  `libCryptography_SOURCES` **unconditionally**; only `GpgMe++.cpp`
+  (gated by `WITH_GPGMEPP`, itself requiring `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES`) and
+  the Mimetic-based local parser are actually optional. This document
+  previously assumed all of `src/Cryptography/` was Qt5-only and
+  out of scope — wrong. `MessageModel` is the generic MIME-tree delegate
+  used even with crypto verification compiled out, and it needs to build
+  on Qt4. Two real gaps: a missing `#include <vector>` (only ever visible
+  via a transitive include Qt5's header graph happened to provide), and a
+  `QMetaObject::Connection` member (doesn't exist on Qt4) used to later
+  `disconnect()` a signal — replaced with the classic 4-argument
+  `disconnect(sender, SIGNAL, receiver, SLOT)`, which needs no `#if` guard
+  since the connect side already uses `SIGNAL()`/`SLOT()` strings.
+  `GpgMe++.h` has the identical `QMetaObject::Connection` pattern but
+  **is** legitimately out of scope, since `GpgMe++.cpp` only enters the
+  build when `WITH_GPGMEPP` is ON.
+- **Lesson for whoever continues iterating on build errors**: treat every
+  compiler error as a prompt to grep-sweep for siblings of the same class
+  of gap (a missed macro/pattern tends to have 2-8 siblings, as
+  `QByteArrayLiteral` and the `connect (` whitespace case showed), and
+  double check whether a `WITH_X`-gated directory actually gates *all* its
+  files before assuming something is out of scope — `WITH_CRYPTO_MESSAGES`
+  did not.
+
 ## Completeness checklist (grep-based, per `QT4-BACKPORT-TASK.md`)
 
